            <ArticleTitle>Orally active ghrelin receptor inverse agonists and their actions on a rat obesity model.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4792-803</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmc.2015.05.047</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0968-0896(15)00457-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of 2-alkylamino nicotinamide analogs was prepared as orally active ghrelin receptor (ghrelinR) inverse agonists. Starting from compound 1, oral bioavailability was improved by modifying metabolically unstable sites and reducing molecular weight. Brain-permeable compound 33 and compound 24 with low brain permeability were tested in rat models of obesity; 30 mg/kg of compound 33 suppressed weight gain. PK/PD analysis revealed that the anti-obesity effect of ghrelinR inverse agonists depends on their brain concentrations.</AbstractText>
